      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this chapter, I go through the very basic methods for isolating and setting up a microalgae culture. Isolation can be done from local algal strains with a micropipette and microscope. Determining algal growth is important and can be done by counting cells under a microscope or by determining the change in dry weight (DW)."},
